Z||000000||Spektrum-87GT||11-06-2001||07:15 PM||||ok, some may not know it, but i'm somewhat of an artist. you also may not know that i have some of the craziest off the wall ideas ever(just ask blackstang about my wooden roller coaster and my electronic engine designs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) anywho, a few years ago i saw a pic of fords gt90 concept. being the huge exotic car fan i was(and still am) i went through the roof, it was all i would talk about for weeks. well, now i'm a little older, a little wiser(ok... not really), and a lot crazier with my ideas. i was thinking of 3d modeling a new fiero kit car similar to the gt90, only updated and rearranged with new ideas. all that i'm asking from you... is support and when i get in a technical pinch(mainly during the design phase). alright, you're probably wondering what kind of credentials i have. well... i work as a 3d modeler/designer and came really close to going to art school for 3d animation/modeling. I've worked with fiberglass in the past, although not on this scale. I've got access to one heck of a welder if need be, i also own a small one. I've put my fiero modifications on hold, mainly because I'm using it as my daily driver, but this is the perfect opportunity to do this. here a few of the off the wall ideas i have for this kit, tell me what you think:<P>shorten the front<BR>stretch the passanger compartment<BR>stretch the engine compartment<BR>if possible, widen the frame a few inches.<BR>aircraft cockpit style sliding door(this one is going to take some explaining, just know that it can be taken off to make a roadster)<BR>3 person seating similar to the mclaren f1<P>they're just too many wierdo ideas to explain, i'll post the website this weekend.||||reg||1
